+ * makes the log self-identifying (hz/10 cadence with sweetlogfast=1) and makes
+ * this bring-up print, pause, then touch the risky register, so the last
+ * durable line names the access that wedged the machine. Its write before the
+ * first sleep, though, stalled this boot at UFS init itself (log43 stops at
+ * the log banner, flush #1, 7234 B), so 0103 goes back to sleeping first and
+ * keeps only the fast cadence and the markers.
